y possibly-AI phrase ('as the models accelerate') is too ambiguous (could mean business models) to establish AI subject per grounding rules.", "video_id": "2094872636996165632"}, {"candidate_paths": [], "disposition": "still_unmapped", "evidence": [], "existing_shelf_ids": [], "reason": "Pure technical/options trading jargon (swing highs, smart-money zones) about CoreWeave stock; never establishes AI as the subject even though the ticker is an AI-cloud company.", "video_id": "2094906875976232960"}, {"candidate_paths": [], "disposition": "still_unmapped", "evidence": [], "existing_shelf_ids": [], "reason": "Same technical stock-trading pattern (CIFR); no AI-establishing text in the excerpt.", "video_id": "2094908776167948288"}, {"candidate_paths": [], "disposition": "unsupported", "evidence": [], "existing_shelf_ids": [], "reason": "Excerpt is untranslated Russian song lyrics; the 'AI' framing appears only in the tweet hook/hint, not in the excerpt text itself.", "video_id": "2094915663961661513"}]}, {"candidates": [{"definition": "Practical guidance and firsthand accounts about finding employment, launching or running an independent business or creative career, and the work habits and non-traditional paths that sustain them.", "exclude": ["general AI industry financial or market news without a personal career or small-business frame (see AI Industry and Market Economics)", "celebrity interviews focused on societal or philosophical commentary rather than career practice", "general technical tutorials aimed at skill-building rather than career or business strategy (see AI and ML \u003e Education)"], "include": ["job search and hiring practices (e.g., avoiding do-not-hire lists, mass-application pitfalls)", "solopreneur and indie-business daily routines (shipping products, validating ideas)", "non-traditional or self-taught paths into a technical career", "financial and business advice for creative professionals and artists", "work ethic and competitive drive as a professional habit", "startup-founding advice from experienced founders"], "path": ["Career and Entrepreneurship"], "sibling_cues": [{"confusing_alternative": "AI Industry and Market Economics (AI talent market as an industry trend)", "evidence_needed": "quote frames it as an individual job-seeker's tactic or consequence, not an industry-wide labor trend", "include_cue": "job search and hiring practices"}, {"confusing_alternative": "AI and ML \u003e Developer Tools (using an AI coding tool to build something)", "evidence_needed": "quote describes a personal work routine or product-shipping mindset, not a specific AI tool's features or workflow", "include_cue": "solopreneur and indie-business daily routines"}, {"confusing_alternative": "AI and ML \u003e Education (step-by-step technical tutorial)", "evidence_needed": "quote narrates someone's career backstory or credentials, not a lesson teaching a skill", "include_cue": "non-traditional or self-taught paths into a technical career"}, {"confusing_alternative": "general music or entertainment commentary", "evidence_needed": "quote gives concrete business or financial guidance (timing, spending, deals) rather than artistic or cultural critique", "include_cue": "financial and business advice for creative professionals and artists"}, {"confusing_alternative": "celebrity biography or psychology commentary", "evidence_needed": "quote ties the drive explicitly to work output or professional operating mode, not personal psychology alone", "include_cue": "work ethic and competitive drive as a professional habit"}, {"confusing_alternative": "AI Industry and Market Economics (a founder discussing company financial metrics)", "evidence_needed": "quote gives generalizable founding/startup advice, not a specific company's revenue or market figures", "include_cue": "startup-founding advice from experienced founders"}], "supporting_evidence": [{"card_hash": "f0408b18213c30302e9728a011fc267af9cee85d4d1475be68eac23baea8ec76", "excerpt_id": "5efbf435ed298e48f009033f6c7fe783feb1a16bfb2ba0b9817cd57607d81b88", "quote": "Mass applying is one of the fastest ways for you to get onto the do not call list", "source_revision": "51d24779d52b75025e22d393789f7c9b5e573efeee39efe598539c163929aa26", "video_id": "4OmEbeR3BtI"}, {"card_hash": "6e7394f38a883dd0cb4dfd220dfcf8a18a23af1ffd91cdbbacc9023a34261150", "excerpt_id": "9f65bd202616e157e2f299e342d10d54e111c2e0edaa9eb0cafb1ec83ded814c", "quote": "I have a big list of things I have to make. So I have a few apps that are already running", "source_revision": "de2771dc015b237c38781356de805a65ad3b19f870bb78632e95549e8cf3a7c8", "video_id": "D4fkiQfzw_I"}, {"card_hash": "62c9fa6eefdd854337411009b3b9d5ff3da74b5c9f443bc87135b4c2c0969a48", "excerpt_id": "7cd15bbeb976e66e5de1e4a8afcf781cab953fef0aaec565d5c9a0a785ec0b6f", "quote": "He doesn't have the normal credentials, right? He did like um he's self-taught as a programmer", "source_revision": "2c880b210c2584b8aa1aa6e326ceea7637cad384452b66605cbdc1530b0e3e93", "video_id": "F97xOWNph5A"}, {"card_hash": "cdef365dba8c8b28e33c07e8d122d90e982c37b769fe0f3289830bc7c838b5fe", "excerpt_id": "9f595d903b17d10b42eca78537a8374c7ab38e25fb3b6b0c5f25c446d6671a99", "quote": "But give yourself time. If you spend a year recording the music, don't put it out in a month.", "source_revision": "809c55ba7c740acdc6a92870492173dcd455b377ef01e85c8611305e257a2e59", "video_id": "Oi-1Ev1fI74"}, {"card_hash": "5f5b568420945801e30276080c9e3f894ad5c55d1d8dccdc167f551950eb1760", "excerpt_id": "c5899c6070fb40a4790f5232e2a4c86015c1d4ea214407667f507969e1c525d2", "quote": "Pain comes in, work comes out. By the time he had a record deal, that was the only way he knew how to operate.", "source_revision": "7e8bd216f28d2884d7942e48730a3eec4bea72d67051768c3ab919e49d817a72", "video_id": "mL8umz2yvfQ"}, {"card_hash": "7dfed919d3d265eb7946cfb61bdd80b4b16044429974d59309f89b1c5f46592d", "excerpt_id": "e2adb42681dc055c2b9c3a07099a6002c1c860eb3b08f401ac5296afe356a0c3", "quote": "My first interview with @sama, Co-Founder of @OpenAI. 0:04 How to start a startup", "source_revision": "8c7a004deea85e4d4cd711ec917c5a7a5c9214cc65c768b7065a635331cc23e2", "video_id": "x_811cef5397c"}]}, {"definition": "Business, financial, and market coverage of the AI industry, including company revenue, compute costs, hardware market positioning, investment, and talent demand.", "exclude": ["model architecture, capability benchmarks, or technical releases (see Frontier Models)", "personal career or job-search advice framed for an individual (see Career and Entrepreneurship)", "AI safety, cybersecurity, or governance guardrails discussion (see Security)"], "include": ["AI company revenue/ARR figures and financial comparisons between AI labs", "cloud and compute cost economics for running AI at scale", "AI hardware makers' market positioning and stock/investor reaction", "AI industry investment and hyperscaler spending trends", "AI talent market and hiring demand as an industry-wide trend"], "path": ["AI and ML", "AI Industry and Market Economics"], "sibling_cues": [{"confusing_alternative": "AI and ML \u003e Frontier Models (model capability or release news)", "evidence_needed": "quote states a dollar figure, revenue, or financial comparison, not a capability or benchmark claim", "include_cue": "AI company revenue/ARR figures and financial comparisons between AI labs"}, {"confusing_alternative": "AI and ML \u003e Developer Tools (technical how-to for running/deploying models)", "evidence_needed": "quote frames a cost or pricing trend, not step-by-step setup instructions", "include_cue": "cloud and compute cost economics for running AI at scale"}, {"confusing_alternative": "AI and ML \u003e Frontier Models (hardware specs or product capability)", "evidence_needed": "quote references market share, stock reaction, or investor sentiment alongside the product, not just its specs", "include_cue": "AI hardware makers' market positioning and stock/investor reaction"}, {"confusing_alternative": "general non-AI business or finance news", "evidence_needed": "quote explicitly ties the spending or investment to AI compute, hyperscalers, or AI labs", "include_cue": "AI industry investment and hyperscaler spending trends"}, {"confusing_alternative": "Career and Entrepreneurship (one person's job-search tactics)", "evidence_needed": "quote frames a market-wide demand or trend for AI talent, not an individual's application strategy", "include_cue": "AI talent market and hiring demand as an industry-wide trend"}], "supporting_evidence": [{"card_hash": "dda2f996b1d2c8b1d4b87490870f330f51dbd3c8111a383921c48dacafe42037", "excerpt_id": "b942af10c017519716012a066274e3d5cdb1a6bf71df44b899b4c15cd53919c2", "quote": "OpenAI was sitting just shy of $50 billion in ARR", "source_revision": "c346179664933cbcfeb986746f8019556125e3449c5cea733dc4b43bac4e1277", "video_id": "episode_ee13d34d83c"}, {"card_hash": "cd669a7bef8c767824345d811f60bb5dce1a3855072b56d89a31a148235dc07b", "excerpt_id": "e3ef2590d14f96c6ada25f151a3b221ca3ec3051197d71e46185259e853c62d1", "quote": "if you look at Nvidia they're probably the best positioned player", "source_revision": "1878e89cad2f73714ed9b3fb6f62b8e1f6d9e68b295082fd04bf924e32d16c3a", "video_id": "_KNjASionIo"}, {"card_hash": "b57fab1d58138e2c2920d5f9849988ae5877a3ac0879da6e9842961f70c62a60", "excerpt_id": "5ab2cac902fbdabd9ccccf0c3015d9dd207dd83b5b402d95ca01b1d5d32a0f23", "quote": "there was going back to their Roots the GPU for the game and there was so much more but the stock doesn't like it", "source_revision": "6213fdf02bbe12e2701a45ae27aa9289094176c90239d3109eb7d8b25ed31139", "video_id": "R6w5MBk1PsM"}, {"card_hash": "9fc0e1707ea088c5552ca39afaff271f767fb3349ff8fd8294ccfd66805b7000", "excerpt_id": "e7f42c35e5ba01cdb169c3f0bd0795ff8895bd943a4627a421b48a6ab5333d3d", "quote": "OpenAI President Greg Brockman explains why Anthropic pulled ahead of OpenAI on ARR", "source_revision": "c0d7a723fa34faa9de27a2f89932023e1809a3540a194942147dee94fec04f95", "video_id": "x_916a6278802"}, {"card_hash": "5df198efd5977afd2486c1cacc1b5629b6da56de8d8fabde28e73facc1898cd2", "excerpt_id": "959916ff9b8a1992fc2b23794b14ed4c43f505cdd29e0aab6cd86933acbea2e6", "quote": "if you're like either AI native or like you buy into it completely, it's crazy. People want you yesterday. When can you start?", "source_revision": "78691a903a2f24773f7aa798ca7f38ac08643870926c014ddd6ada45e4a79a22", "video_id": "pBF05PNBmJA"}]}], "dispositions": [{"candidate_paths": [["Career and Entrepreneurship"]], "disposition": "proposed_concept", "evidence": [{"card_hash": "f0408b18213c30302e9728a011fc267af9cee85d4d1475be68eac23baea8ec76", "excerpt_id": "5efbf435ed298e48f009033f6c7fe783feb1a16bfb2ba0b9817cd57607d81b88", "quote": "Mass applying is one of the fastest ways for you to get onto the do not call list", "source_revision": "51d24779d52b75025e22d393789f7c9b5e573efeee39efe598539c163929aa26", "video_id": "4OmEbeR3BtI"}], "existing_shelf_ids": [], "reason": "Concrete job-search and hiring-list advice fits the Career and Entrepreneurship candidate's job-search cue.", "video_id": "4OmEbeR3BtI"}, {"candidate_paths": [["Career and Entrepreneurship"]], "disposition": "proposed_concept", "evidence": [{"card_hash": "6e7394f38a883dd0cb4dfd220dfcf8a18a23af1ffd91cdbbacc9023a34261150", "excerpt_id": "9f65bd202616e157e2f299e342d10d54e111c2e0edaa9eb0cafb1ec83ded814c", "quote": "I have a big list of things I have to make. So I have a few apps that are already running", "source_revision": "de2771dc015b237c38781356de805a65ad3b19f870bb78632e95549e8cf3a7c8", "video_id": "D4fkiQfzw_I"}], "existing_shelf_ids": [], "reason": "Solopreneur product-shipping routine matches the indie-business-routine cue.", "video_id": "D4fkiQfzw_I"}, {"candidate_paths": [["Career and Entrepreneurship"]], "disposition": "proposed_concept", "evidence": [{"card_hash": "62c9fa6eefdd854337411009b3b9d5ff3da74b5c9f443bc87135b4c2c0969a48", "excerpt_id": "7cd15bbeb976e66e5de